<title>INDIA: POLL- MTNL 6-mth net seen higher.</title>
<headline>POLL- MTNL 6-mth net seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net profit of Mahanagar Telephone Nigam Ltd (MTNL) is forecast to improve 15.1 percent to 5.0 billion rupees in the first six months of fiscal 1997/98 (April-March), a Reuter poll consensus showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>MTNL is a state-run telephone monopoly in Bombay and Delhi. Its sales are seen rising 6.5 percent to 20.9 billion rupees, according to the consensus estimate of 18 leading brokerages.</p>
<p>Following are the details of the poll compared with actuals for the first half of 1996/97.</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>				NET PROFIT		   SALES</p>
<p>				   (first half to September 30)</p>
<p>			    97/98     96/97	97/98	96/97</p>
<p>					 (in millions of rupees)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>MTNL   ----PAT seen up 15.1%, sales up 6.5%</p>
<p>Average		5,022.40  4,362.40    20,905.80  19,622.50</p>
<p>High		   5,900.00		  24,013.50</p>
<p>Low		    4,750.00		  20,800.00</p>
<p>--Bombay equities desk +91-22-265-9000</p>
